    "content": "<p>Distributed teams are international by default — but most meeting tools still assume everyone shares one language. <strong>VoxTranslate for Business</strong> removes that barrier for your whole organization: each person speaks their own language, everyone else reads and hears the conversation in theirs, and the call is saved with a searchable, translatable transcript.</p><h2>The hidden cost of the language barrier</h2><p>When part of a team works in a second language, meetings slow down, quieter voices stay quiet, and decisions get revisited. Interpreters are expensive and don't scale to daily stand-ups, so the friction becomes a tax on collaboration that rarely shows up on any budget line.</p><h2>A workspace built for multilingual teams</h2><p>VoxTranslate for Business adds an organization layer on top of real-time translated calls:</p><ul><li><strong>Team workspace</strong> — organize calls by project and keep full, searchable history for your whole org.</li><li><strong>Multilingual transcripts</strong> — every recorded call is transcribed with speaker labels and translatable into 84 languages on demand.</li><li><strong>Cloud recording</strong> — record calls to your private workspace instead of a personal download.</li><li><strong>Privacy &amp; compliance</strong> — an audit log, configurable data retention, and EU storage for regulated teams.</li></ul><h2>How it works</h2><p>Create an organization, invite your team by email, and group your calls into projects. Start a meeting from any browser — no installs — and everyone joins in their own language. When a call ends, its recording is transcribed automatically and appears in your history, ready to read, translate, or export.</p><h2>Pricing that fits a team</h2><p>Plans are priced per organization, not per seat: <strong>Business</strong> from €49/month and <strong>Enterprise</strong> from €199/month, both with monthly credits, transcripts, and unlimited history included. Subscriptions renew automatically and can be cancelled anytime.</p><h2>Try it with your team</h2><p>Set up your workspace in minutes, invite a few colleagues, and run your next international meeting with everyone in their own language.</p>",
